{"step_index":115,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:03:33Z","thinking":"**Refining Login Page and Credentials**\n\nRevised the login page title to \"Authorized Access Portal Login\" or \"Verifier, Institution & Admin Authentication\" for clarity and broader user understanding. Demo credentials will be updated to include \"Fill: Verifier / Employer\" with the username \"verifier\" and password \"Verifier@12345\". Incorporated support for a \"notice\" query parameter, displaying a specific message when \"verify_required\" is present to guide users toward authorized login.\n\n\n**Adding Verifier User and Verification Section**\n\nDetermined the location to seed the verifier user account is within the data initialization process. Created a `ROLE_VERIFIER` user with credentials. Also, identified the section to be added to the UI, specifically within the initial display template. The UI will have elements for verification functionality that are currently hidden.\n\n\n**Restructuring Homepage for Verification**\n\nRemoved the credential verification search card from the welcome page, along with loading indicators and result displays. The welcome page is being updated to highlight authorized portal access. This includes a new section with clear calls to action, such as a launch button for the verification console and a sign-in link.\n\nThe navigation menu's \"Verify Credential\" link has been updated to directly link to the dashboard's verification tab and includes a lock icon. Auth navigation will now display \"Console / Dashboard\" and \"Logout\" when the user is logged in.\n\n\n**Implementing Dashboard Verification Tab**\n\nAdded a new tab to the dashboard for credential verification, incorporating a dedicated button and corresponding tab pane. The tab pane includes a search input field and a button to initiate the verification process. Real-time SHA-256 fingerprint matching and AI-driven fraud heuristic detection are suggested for the functionality.\n\n\n**Designing Credential Verification UI**\n\nDetermined the UI elements for the credential verification process. Specifically, included a dedicated section containing demo test records for demonstration. Added a loading indicator and a result card to be populated after verification attempts.\n\n\n**Analyzing Credential Verification Outcome**\n\nObserved that the verification response includes graduate details such as name, ID, award title, specialization, grade, institution, and conferment date. A tamper-evident SHA-256 fingerprint is also present in the response. Further analysis is needed to parse and display these details effectively in the UI.\n\n\n**Assessing AI Fraud Risk Validation**\n\nThe AI risk assessment indicates low risk with a perfect score. Verified that the data payload remained unmodified, the institution is accredited, and the issuance chronology is authentic.\n\nAudit log and consensus node details were noted for record-keeping. The system confirms an authentic credential.\n\n\n**Adjusting Credential Verification Logic**\n\nAdjusted the initial page display to hide UI elements if the user is a verifier, administrator, or from an institution, defaulting to the verification tab. Enhanced the credential verification function to include the authentication token in the request headers. This facilitates authorized access to credential verification.\n\nModified the dashboard's verification flow to update the verification input field with a certificate number when triggered. This eliminates the need for redirection to a separate verification page, streamlining the user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Verification Redirection**\n\nThe `/verify` endpoint's handling was updated to redirect requests to `/dashboard?tab=verifyTab`. The login page (`login.html`) was modified to include a demo verifier credential button and handling for a `notice=verify_required` query parameter to display a specific message.\n\nThe security configuration permits access to `/dashboard`. This suggests that if the user is not authenticated, they are redirected to the login page from the dashboard as expected.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system\\src\\test\\java\\com\\devops\\qvs\\controller\\VerificationControllerIntegrationTest.java","EndLine":80,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing VerificationControllerIntegrationTest.java","toolSummary":"Check verification tests"}}]}
